# SCM syntax highlighting & preventing 3-way merges
# pixi.lock is machine-generated and ~10k lines. `merge=binary` stops git from
# attempting a three-way merge on it: a conflict there is never worth resolving
# by hand - take one side and re-run `pixi lock` against the merged manifest.
# The linguist hints keep it out of the repo's language statistics and collapse
# it in GitHub diffs.
pixi.lock merge=binary linguist-language=YAML linguist-generated=true

# Notebooks are LF-normalised JSON, which is what the nbstripout pre-commit hook
# and the CI `notebooks` task produce. Without this pin a Windows checkout
# rewrites every line, so every notebook under `docs/examples/` shows up as a
# full-file diff.
*.ipynb text eol=lf

# The committed LAS/LAZ fixtures are binary: never touch their line endings.
*.las binary
*.laz binary
